{"id":"wikibooks:cola-cake","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3ACola_Cake","status":"fixed","reason":"Conversion template lost baking temperature","ingredients":["2 cups (275 g / 9.7 oz) flour","2 cups (450 g / 16 oz) white granulated sugar","1 cup (250 ml / 8.5 oz) cola","2 sticks (250 g / 8.8 oz / 1 cup) margarine","3 tablespoons cocoa","2 eggs","½ cup (125 ml / 4.2 oz) buttermilk","½ teaspoon baking soda","1 teaspoon vanilla extract","1 ½ cup (125 g / 4.4 oz) miniature marshmallows","6 tablespoons cola","2 tablespoons cocoa","1 stick (125 g / 4.4 oz) margarine","1 teaspoon vanilla","4 cups (500 g / 1.1 lb) powdered sugar","1 cup (80 g / 2.8 oz) chopped nuts (optional)"],"steps":["Combine flour and sugar in a bowl.","Mix cola, margarine, and cocoa in a saucepan, and bring to a boil.","Pour over flour/sugar mixture and mix well.","Beat the eggs and mix them in. Add milk, soda, vanilla and marshmallows to make thin batter. Marshmallows will float to the surface.","Bake in a 9x13-inch (23x33 cm) pan at 350°F for 35 minutes. Make frosting before it cools.","Mix cola, cocoa, and margarine in a pan and bring to a boil.","Add vanilla, sugar, and nuts. Mix until smooth.","Spread the warm frosting on the cake."]}]}
